      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain-boundary strengthening contributes to the increase in compressive strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb, Mo, Cr, Ti, and Al have lower tendencies to form long-lived neutron-activation products than tungsten.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selecting Nb, Mo, Cr, Ti, and Al reduces the composite's overall neutron activation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The NbMoCrTiAl composite will have superior high-temperature oxidation resistance.",
